# Source-vs-deployed drift, daily. The class a commit-time gate cannot see: /etc is
# hand-edited (or a unit is installed and never committed) between commits, and
# bin/auto-sync commits and pushes every 15 minutes without ever calling verify.sh
# (bin/auto-sync:32-34), so "the gate runs when a human commits" is not true on this box.
#
# ExecStart points at the SOURCE repo, which inverts the convention every other job here
# follows, deliberately. This job's subject IS the relationship between the trees, so a copy
# of it exec'd out of the runtime tree resolves its own REPO to that tree: source and runtime
# become one directory, the bin comparison reports zero findings whatever the repo contains,
# and design/ — which bin/deploy does not ship — is absent, so every /etc-only unit reads as
# undeclared drift. Measured 2026-09-02: a tautology in one half and 11 false findings in the
# other, alerting daily. The checker now refuses both shapes rather than trusting this line.
[Unit]
Description=Source-vs-deployed drift check (four unit trees) — D8
OnFailure=agent-alert@%n.service

[Service]
Type=oneshot
User=dave
Environment=DELIVERY_JOB=%n
ExecStart=/home/dave/dev/agent-workforce/bin/check_deploy_drift.sh
TimeoutStartSec=5min
NoNewPrivileges=true
